{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-83708" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $A$ for which ${\\lambda }_{1}=2,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=-3,$ ${\\lambda }_{3}=1$ are eigenvalues, and \n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nare the respective eigenvectors. Find the matrices $P$ and $D$ such that $PD{P}^{-1}=A,$ where $D$ is a diagonal matrix." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069769/state.json" "file_sha256" "51482139b12ad11076951f5931a809c855e61cc5579dbeb014250b66c90a3146"} {"question" "q-83708" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the eigenvalues of the matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=2,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=-3,$ ${\\lambda }_{3}=1,$ we construct the diagonal matrix $D$ by writing the eigenvalues in the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, to construct the matrix $P,$ we simply write the respective eigenvectors as columns: \n\n- the $1$st column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{1}=2,$\n\n- the $2$nd column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{2}=-3,$ and\n\n- the $3$rd column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{3}=1.$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069769/state.json" "file_sha256" "51482139b12ad11076951f5931a809c855e61cc5579dbeb014250b66c90a3146"} {"question" "q-83708" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-worke